stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Launch

  Launch --> Preflight: meridian tui
  Preflight --> Bail: not a TTY / TERM=dumb / terminal too small
  Bail --> [*]: print the equivalent headless CLI command, exit 1

  Preflight --> Onboarding: no account.json in MERIDIAN_HOME
  Preflight --> Unlock: account exists, file-backed store
  Preflight --> Main: account exists, OS keystore

  state Onboarding {
    [*] --> ChooseStore
    ChooseStore --> OrgHint: OS keystore or passphrase keyfile
    OrgHint --> Generate: enter the @domain hint
    Generate --> ShowIdentity: Ed25519 keypair minted via meridian-identity
    ShowIdentity --> Register: mrd1 ID plus QR shown, copy or save
    Register --> PublishBundle: connect to rendezvous, optional invite token
    PublishBundle --> [*]: prekey bundle published
    note right of ShowIdentity
      The private key never leaves the
      SecretStore and is never rendered.
    end note
  }
  Onboarding --> Main: registered

  Unlock --> Main: passphrase accepted
  Unlock --> Unlock: wrong passphrase, retry with attempt count
  Unlock --> [*]: user quits

  state Main {
    [*] --> Conversation
    Conversation --> Contacts: Tab
    Contacts --> Conversation: Enter on a contact
    Contacts --> AddContact: n
    AddContact --> Contacts: paste mrd1 ID or import QR, assign a local petname
    Contacts --> Requests: r
    Requests --> Contacts: accept promotes to pinned, reject drops the request
    Contacts --> Verify: v
    Verify --> Contacts: safety numbers match, mark verified or block
    Conversation --> Diagnostics: palette
    Diagnostics --> Conversation: Esc
    Conversation --> Settings: palette
    Settings --> Conversation: Esc
  }

  Main --> Help: F1
  Help --> Main: Esc
  Main --> Palette: Ctrl-K
  Palette --> Main: Esc or run a command

  Main --> KeyChangeWarning: pinned contact key changed
  KeyChangeWarning --> Main: acknowledged, contact re-pinned
  KeyChangeWarning --> Main: Verify is the primary action, opens the Verify screen

  Main --> KeyChangeBlocked: VERIFIED contact key or device record changed
  KeyChangeBlocked --> Main: re-verified out of band, sends resume
  KeyChangeBlocked --> Blocked: user blocks the contact
  Blocked --> Main: contact stays blocked, sends refused
  note right of KeyChangeBlocked
    Composer is DISABLED. No dismiss,
    no trust-anyway, no timed accept.
    Wording is canonical per
    security/verification-ux.md.
  end note

  Main --> Quit: Ctrl-Q
  Quit --> Main: cancelled, unsent input preserved
  Quit --> [*]: terminal restored by the RAII guard
